            rows: 5,
            frames: 20,
            frames_per_second: 10.0,
            alt: "a newly built four-block ship running past a rock under its own drive",
        ),
        body: "Test a new ship before using it in a scenario. Accelerate to speed, then use STOP. This shows how quickly the ship accelerates and how much room it needs to slow down.",
        wiki_path: "wiki/flight-autopilot#the-hull-decides-the-handling",
        field_notes: [
            "Test a new ship to learn how quickly it accelerates and stops.",
        ],
    )),
    Lesson((
        id: "build_stacking",
        category: Shipbuilding,
        order: 50,
        title: "A second flight computer",
        media: Image(
            image: "self://training/build_stacking.webp",
            alt: "two flight computers on one spine in the editor, both of them listed in the scene tree, and the rail naming the structure as what holds the turn rate down",
        ),
        body: "Most ships are already limited by their structure, so another flight computer does not make them turn faster. It improves turning precision and keeps the ship controllable if another computer is destroyed.",
        wiki_path: "wiki/sections/controller#stacking-controllers",
        field_notes: [
            "Extra flight computers improve precision and provide a backup.",
        ],
    )),
    Lesson((
        id: "build_weapon_mounts",
        category: Shipbuilding,
        order: 60,
        title: "Where a weapon can point",
        media: Image(
            image: "self://training/build_weapon_mounts.webp",
            alt: "a turret bolted on a hull\'s top face and a railgun on its nose, the turret\'s card open in the inspector",
        ),
        body: "A turret can aim in most directions but cannot aim below its mount. A railgun cannot turn and only fires outward from the hull face where it is mounted.",
        wiki_path: "wiki/sections/turret#what-it-can-bear-on",
        field_notes: [
            "Weapon placement determines where the weapon can fire.",
        ],
    )),
    Lesson((
        id: "build_docking_port",
        category: Shipbuilding,
        order: 70,
        title: "Bolting on a docking port",
        media: Image(
            image: "self://training/build_docking_port.webp",
            alt: "a docking port seated on a hull face in the editor, its capture envelope open in the inspector",
        ),
        body: "Base ships do not include docking ports, so you must add one before a ship can dock. Keep the port\'s hatch facing outward and clear of other sections.",
        wiki_path: "wiki/sections/docking#variants",
        field_notes: [
            "A ship needs a docking port before it can dock.",
        ],
    )),
    Lesson((
        id: "build_dock_envelope",
        category: Shipbuilding,
        order: 75,
        title: "Making a dock",
        media: Loop(
            sheet: "self://training/build_dock_envelope.webp",
