            rows: 5,
            frames: 20,
            frames_per_second: 10.0,
            alt: "a tender lining up on a moored spar: the docking sight\'s face plates square up and go green, then the gap line as the hull brakes inside the capture distance, and a DOCK chip joins the verb row",
        ),
        body: "To dock, bring the ports within 10 meters, face them toward each other, and reduce the ships\' relative movement and spin. Once docked, your ship\'s steering and thrusters are disabled.",
        actions: [
            "dock",
        ],
        wiki_path: "wiki/sections/docking#flying-the-approach",
        field_notes: [
            "Docking requires two aligned ports and very little relative movement.",
        ],
    )),
    Lesson((
        id: "build_skin",
